<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S4-005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S4-005" ;
  triage:title "Production daemon auto-start thread::sleep(poll_interval) not documented as accepted Anti-Flake exception (composition.rs:254)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm/src/composition.rs:254-268 — DaemonSupervisor::ensure_daemon_available_with_lock_path uses thread::sleep(poll_interval) in a production polling loop while waiting for daemon to start after auto-start. Sprint S.4 coverage audit did not document this as an accepted exception to the anti-flake contract. plan-phase-S.md §4.1 does not record it as an accepted production polling exception. This is almost certainly a legitimate accepted pattern (waiting for external process launch has no push-based notification surface; bounded polling is required), but the exception is undocumented. Fix: document explicitly in plan-phase-S.md §4.1 as an accepted production exception with rationale. If emit_ready_signal_if_requested provides a readiness-signal mechanism that can be read by the CLI, wire it up as the preferred alternative." ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-09T18:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-S4-005/s4/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/feature-pS-s4-hardening/dd36874> .

